vs our old code:

```python
def add_content(self, more_content, no_docstring=False):
    if self.doc_as_attr:
        try:
            more_content = StringList([_('alias of %s') % restify(self.object)], source='')
        except AttributeError:
            pass
    super().add_content(more_content)
```

The modern one only sets the "alias of" content when there's no variable comment (doccomment) — i.e., `not self.get_variable_comment()`. That's the fix for #9236: when a doccomment exists for the alias, show the doccomment instead of (or rather, don't override more_content with) "alias of ...".

